---
/**
 * THE BRAND MARKS, INLINE, BECAUSE A DESIGN SYSTEM DOES NOT SHIP THEM.
 *
 * MEASURED: `@akhil-saxena/design-system/icons` exports 32 wrappers and not one is a brand mark —
 * no GitHub, no LinkedIn, no Mail. lucide v1 dropped the brand set and Fontshare has nothing to
 * mirror, so this is a real absence rather than an oversight (05-09 filed it).
 *
 * That absence is also CORRECT. A design system's icons are UI primitives — chevrons, checks,
 * a search glass. GitHub's logo is a third party's trademark, versioned by them and licensed by
 * them; it is content, not a primitive. So this is not a workaround for a gap the library should
 * have filled. It is the app owning something the library should not.
 *
 * `currentColor` throughout, so colour is the caller's and this file originates none — which is
 * what keeps it (T) under QUAL-03 rather than an origination.
 *
 * The paths are the legacy site's own, carried across verbatim: `IconGitHub`, `IconLinkedIn` and
 * `IconMail` from `src/components/icons.tsx` on `legacy/nextjs-portfolio`.
 */
interface Props {
  readonly icon: string;
  readonly size?: number;
}
/*
 * 16, NOT 18. Akhil: *"all 3 icons should be aligned cleanly, similar size."* MEASURED across the
 * page, six icons ship at two sizes: the bar's theme toggle and its two mobile nav glyphs at 16x16,
 * these three at 18x18. The bar's 16 is the number that cannot move — the toggle's optical
 * alignment to the gutter is a `(40 - 16) / 2` pull, and `--space-3` is 12px exactly, so a 17px or
 * 18px glyph would need 11.5px or 11px and neither is a rung. So the footer comes to the bar.
 */
const { icon, size = 16 } = Astro.props;
---

{
  /*
   * ================================================================================================
   * THE STORE MARKS, CARRIED FROM THE LEGACY APP — NOT REDRAWN
   * ================================================================================================
   *
   * `Final Split Variations.html` docks a row of destination marks under each project icon. The
   * design system exports THIRTY-THREE icons and not one is a GitHub, a Play Store, a Chrome Store
   * or an outbound arrow — MEASURED against `dist/icons/index.d.ts`, whose entire export list is UI
   * glyphs: chevrons, a check, a trash, a sun and a moon. That is D-28, the finding that the system
   * ships no brand marks, and it is why this file exists at all.
   *
   * 🔴 THESE PATHS ARE THE LEGACY APP'S OWN, taken verbatim from
   * `legacy/nextjs-portfolio:src/components/icons.tsx` — `IconPlayStore`, `IconChromeStore` and
   * `IconArrowUpRight`. Akhil: *"fetch play store, gh, web, chrome web store icons etc from legacy
   * app."* My first pass drew them by hand: a triangle-ish play shape and a puzzle piece standing in
   * for the Chrome Store. Both were wrong as BRANDS — Google Play is a four-facet triangle with a
   * seam and the Chrome Web Store is Chrome's own trilobe, and neither is something to approximate
   * on a page whose job is to look like the work is real. The same argument as the GitHub and
   * LinkedIn paths below, which were carried across for exactly this reason.
   *
   * FILL, NOT STROKE, on the two brand marks, because that is how they are drawn — `makeIcon`'s
   * second argument in the legacy file is `"currentColor"` for both, which switches it from a
   * stroked glyph to a filled one. Stroking a filled path renders an outline of the silhouette,
   * which is a different mark.
   *
   * `arrow-up-right` IS NOT A BRAND and lives here anyway: it is what a project with no store uses
   * — Cairn and the design system, both simply live on the web — and putting one glyph in its own
   * file to satisfy a category would be worse than the slightly narrow name on this one.
   */
  /*
   * THE WEB GLOBE, from `legacy/nextjs-portfolio:public/globe.svg`. Akhil: *"use web globe instead
   * of arrow icon in cairn."* The arrow it replaces was `IconArrowUpRight` — a generic "goes
   * somewhere else" mark, which is what every link on the page does; a globe says the somewhere is
   * the open web, which is the one thing Cairn's dock has to distinguish it from a store listing.
   *
   * ==============================================================================================
   * TRACED FROM ARTWORK AKHIL SUPPLIED, NOT DRAWN HERE
   * ==============================================================================================
   *
   * Akhil, after four rounds of me drawing one: *"use —Pngtree—globe vector icon_3730776 in
   * downloads folder."*
   *
   * ── WHY IT IS A PATH AND NOT AN `<img>` ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   *
   * The source is a 1007x1007 RGBA PNG of flat black on transparent. Dropping it in as an `<img>`
   * beside the other marks would have shipped a mark that CANNOT TAKE THE THEME: every other glyph
   * here paints with `currentColor`, and `.wk-mark-link` sets that from `--ink-4`, so a black raster
   * would have been invisible on the dark ground the site opens in. A CSS `mask-image` would
   * recolour it, but it means 34KB of raster for a 16px glyph plus a paint step. A path is 1.8KB and
   * inherits colour for free.
   *
   * ── HOW IT WAS TRACED, SINCE NOTHING ON THIS MACHINE TRACES ────────────────────────────────
   *
   * No potrace, no ImageMagick, no Inkscape. PIL is present, and the source is a clean two-colour
   * bitmap, so the trace is EXACT rather than an approximation of a photograph:
   *
   *   1. ink = (255 - luminance) * alpha / 255. BOTH channels are needed — luminance alone reads the
   *      transparent surround as ink, because transparent pixels are stored black.
   *   2. cropped to the ink's own bbox (121,121)-(888,888), so the glyph fills its viewBox instead
   *      of inheriting the source file's 12% margin.
   *   3. resampled to 320x320 with LANCZOS, which hands marching squares a CONTINUOUS field — the
   *      resample does the smoothing, so no blur pass was needed.
   *   4. marching squares at 0.5, segments joined into 20 closed rings.
   *   5. Douglas-Peucker at tolerance 1.1, giving 171 points and 1.8KB.
   *
   * 🔴 THE RINGS ARE SPLIT BEFORE SIMPLIFYING. A closed ring's first and last point coincide, so
   * Douglas-Peucker measures every distance against a ZERO-LENGTH baseline and returns two points —
   * the first run produced a 235-byte path for twenty rings, which is how the bug announced itself.
   * Each ring is now split at the point farthest from its start and the two open chains are
   * simplified separately.
   *
   * 🔴 AND THERE ARE 20 SEPARATE RINGS, NOT ONE WITH HOLES. The grid lines cut the disc into
   * disconnected patches, so `fill-rule="evenodd"` is not doing hole arithmetic here — it is just the
   * safe choice if a future trace does produce nesting.
   *
   * Tolerances 0.4 (3.4KB), 0.7 (2.5KB), 1.1 (1.8KB) and 1.6 (1.4KB) were rendered at 16px and 96px
   * on both grounds. 1.1 is the smallest that is indistinguishable from 0.4 at either size.
   *
   * ⚠️ PROVENANCE: this is Pngtree artwork. Their free tier asks for attribution and restricts
   * redistribution, and a traced derivative is still a derivative. Flagged for Akhil rather than
   * decided here. If it has to go, the fallback is on the record: lucide's `globe` at stroke 2.6 read
   * cleanly at 16px and was the runner-up, rejected only for being line art among filled neighbours.
   *
   * Five hand-drawn arrangements were rejected before this and are written down so none is retried:
   * straight bars (a grid, not a sphere); one lens meridian (a blob at 16px); two parallels plus two
   * meridians (a checkerboard); axis plus equator plus a thin pair (holes 1.1px wide at 16px, so
   * they greyed out entirely); and lucide `earth`, whose continent paths read as a face.
   */
  icon === 'globe' && (
    <svg width={size} height={size} viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M11.47,-0.01 10.95,0.21 10.5,0.6 9.59,1.95 8.76,4.12 8.16,6.83 11.47,7.09 15.28,6.9 14.72,4.2 13.67,1.57 13.22,0.9 12.6,0.28 12.0,-0.01ZM10.57,16.87 8.18,17.09 8.32,18.0 9.05,20.7 9.97,22.65 10.95,23.72 11.47,23.95 12.0,23.95 12.53,23.71 12.97,23.32 13.91,21.9 14.72,19.73 15.31,17.1 13.12,16.86ZM7.8,12.37 7.86,14.55 8.1,16.29 11.7,16.04 15.42,16.2 15.66,12.38ZM13.8,0.28 14.56,1.57 15.17,3.0 16.12,6.8 18.0,6.47 19.5,6.05 18.7,4.35 17.25,2.48 15.68,1.17ZM16.12,17.14 15.17,20.93 14.57,22.35 13.8,23.66 15.6,22.82 17.02,21.69 18.47,19.95 19.53,18.0 19.5,17.88 18.3,17.54ZM8.1,7.65 7.86,9.38 7.8,11.57 15.68,11.55 15.61,9.53 15.38,7.7 11.4,7.9ZM7.05,17.24 5.33,17.61 3.96,18.07 4.99,19.95 6.38,21.63 8.1,22.96 9.68,23.66 8.89,22.35 8.23,20.77 7.38,17.25ZM9.45,0.35 7.88,1.11 6.21,2.48 4.85,4.2 3.98,5.87 5.33,6.32 7.35,6.72 8.16,3.38 8.82,1.73 9.66,0.38ZM16.88,1.03 18.85,3.15 20.32,5.74 21.69,5.1 21.75,5.03 21.18,4.28 19.57,2.69 18.07,1.63ZM3.67,6.64 2.99,9.0 2.74,11.55 6.95,11.55 7.24,7.58ZM2.77,12.36 2.76,13.2 2.98,14.93 3.67,17.29 5.4,16.78 7.2,16.41 6.93,12.38ZM20.32,18.19 18.91,20.7 17.85,21.98 16.96,22.8 17.02,22.85 18.23,22.21 19.57,21.25 20.65,20.25 21.71,18.98 21.52,18.74ZM19.73,6.81 16.22,7.65 16.5,11.55 20.72,11.55 20.43,8.78 19.88,6.83ZM16.57,12.36 16.48,12.45 16.27,16.35 19.88,17.12 20.49,14.85 20.71,12.38ZM22.12,5.76 20.61,6.53 21.24,8.78 21.54,11.47 21.6,11.57 23.93,11.57 23.8,9.97 23.43,8.4 22.74,6.67 22.29,5.85ZM21.6,12.36 21.24,15.15 20.61,17.4 22.2,18.2 22.89,16.95 23.5,15.3 23.79,14.03 23.96,12.45 23.85,12.36ZM1.73,5.73 1.04,6.97 0.42,8.62 0.06,10.35 0.0,11.57 1.9,11.55 2.23,8.7 2.9,6.38ZM0.0,12.36 0.06,13.57 0.44,15.38 1.03,16.95 1.73,18.2 2.9,17.55 2.23,15.22 1.92,12.45 1.88,12.36ZM3.15,18.36 2.25,18.82 2.21,18.98 3.9,20.87 5.93,22.35 4.34,20.4ZM5.7,1.72 3.52,3.42 2.38,4.72 2.16,5.03 2.23,5.1 3.23,5.57 4.25,3.67 5.85,1.73Z" />
    </svg>
  )
}
{
  icon === 'play-store' && (
    <svg width={size} height={size} viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M22.018 13.298l-3.919 2.218-3.515-3.493 3.543-3.521 3.891 2.202a1.49 1.49 0 010 2.594zM1.337.924a1.486 1.486 0 00-.112.568v21.017c0 .217.045.419.124.6l11.155-11.087L1.337.924zm12.207 10.065l3.258-3.238L3.45.195a1.466 1.466 0 00-.946-.179l11.04 10.973zm0 2.067l-11 10.933c.298.036.612-.016.906-.183l13.324-7.54-3.23-3.21z" />
    </svg>
